title ALES129 — Lotus's stereo_normalize: peak normalization carried into stereo with one shared gain, the linked normalize that preserves the stereo image
prompt Continue the recurring baton (prin recur) on the ALES/Lotus edge, Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think Fourth lap of this recur run. The stereo pure-rearrangement class stood whole at ALES128 (reverse · rotate · invert · nyquist_flip), each a TRIVIAL per-channel lift because the op touches each seat or value in isolation and the two channels never need to agree on a number. The next Lindy-first crux is the one op where independence would be a BUG: peak normalization (ALES103). Lifting it honestly is the whole point — it opens the stereo AMPLITUDE class and establishes the shared-gain pattern every amplitude lift after it will follow.
think Read normalize.rye (mono: refuse zero/over-ceiling target BadTarget, measure peak through ALES13, silent clip left exactly as is, else gain the whole clip by target/peak through ALES2). The naive stereo lift — normalize each channel to the target independently — would drag the quieter channel's peak up to the target too, collapsing the inter-channel level difference that IS the stereo image. The honest lift is LINKED: measure both channels via meter.measure_stereo, take the LARGER peak (the master peak), scale BOTH channels by the ONE shared fraction target/master_peak. Reused normalize.NormalizeError by name; the union of MeterError, EditError, and BadTarget is exactly right.
think Wrote the design read, module, and witness. Module asserts balance on entry and exit, bound-checks the target before any read, returns on a both-silent master before the division (denominator always the measured non-zero master peak), runs ALES2's gain on each channel over [0,len) with shared num/den. Five laws proven on metal: linked-scale law (each channel == ALES2's gain with the shared denominator, left ×2 and right ×2 for an 8000/4000 master to 16000, not right ×4), master-peak law (master peak == target across four masters — loud-left, loud-right, the domain-ceiling floor, alternating — at five targets), image-preserving law (a 2:1 field to 16000 leaves left 16000 and right 8000, and trips a guard if right ever reaches the target), balance/silence law (equal-length, both-silent and empty pairs unchanged), idempotence law with refusals (twice equals once, zero and over-ceiling targets each refuse BadTarget untouched). Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean.
obs The stereo suite crossed from pure rearrangement into amplitude, and the crossing carried the real lesson: a stereo amplitude op uses ONE shared gain measured across both channels, never a per-channel gain, or the stereo image flattens. The image-preserving law makes that checkable — it proves the 2:1 ratio survives and guards against the naive lift. No custody gate reached — purely local software, self-approved design round.
loom witness=ales_stereo_normalize_witness result=GREEN laws=5 channels=2 masters=4 targets=5
file lotus/stereo_normalize.rye ALES129 — stereo_normalize_peak, the linked stereo normalize: measure both channels, share one gain target/master_peak, five laws with the image-preserving crux.
file tools/ales_stereo_normalize_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-normalize line.
file active-designing/20260815-025919_fill-ales129-lotus-stereo-normalize.md the self-approved design read for this rung.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES129 roster entry and stamp.
recommend keep-going the stereo amplitude class is open; the next mechanical laps lift the remaining value/amplitude ops (fade, halve, rectify) to stereo with the same shared-gain discipline where balance matters — no gate reached.
